## Context contrast (descriptive, not the question asked)

Replication success among junior-lead studies (D2, `seniority.r`): 16/38 = 42.1%;
among senior-lead studies: 19/59 = 32.2%; Fisher exact two-sided p = 0.388 (not significant).

## Data-integrity checks run

* rpp: 97 rows, 97 unique ids, 0 full-row duplicates, 0 duplicate ids; 2 titles appear twice under different ids
  (rpp.49/50, rpp.148/149) -> kept in primary, deduped as sensitivity F4 (n = 95).
* `drop == True` inside rpp = 7 rows (data-quality flags: n.r = 13; n.r = 455,304; missing effect sizes) ->
  kept in primary per decision (d), removed as sensitivity F1 (n = 90).
* seniority categories observed are exactly the 5 documented ones; category counts sum to N on both lines.
* D1 subset of D2 subset of D3 counts hold (23 <= 38 <= 54 on `seniority.r`).
* F2 counts verified integral: 10/35 = 28.6%, 16/35 = 45.7%, 20/35 = 57.1%.
* File B (`..._replication_success_data_...csv`, 143 x 15) has **no seniority field**; its `project == "Psychology"`
  rows (73) surname-match rpp originals 71/73 with median |po - p_value.o| = 2.5e-4, confirming that
  "Psychology" == `project == "rpp"`. It is not used for the numerator or denominator.
